<title>GREECE: Greek ship blast kills two.</title>
<headline>Greek ship blast kills two.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A gas explosion ripped through a Greek ship in the Perama shipyard area west of Athens, killing two people and seriously injuring a number of others, police said.</p>
<p>They said the blast, which blew out windows in shops nearby, was caused by an accident during repair work on the ferry &quot;Evyenia&quot;.</p>
</text>
